Chapter: MagicOracleOverflowTest
  cites Magic chapter OracleParse
  cites Magic chapter Card
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 A number in oracle text too large for an Integer reads as no number, and a
 clause carrying one is unmodelled, never a trap and never a default value.

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("pump small      : " & describe-effect (parse-primary-effect "Target creature gets +3/+3 until end of turn."))
    print-line-uni ("pump huge power : " & describe-effect (parse-primary-effect "Target creature gets +99999999999999999999/+1 until end of turn."))
    print-line-uni ("pump huge tough : " & describe-effect (parse-pump "Target creature gets +1/+99999999999999999999 until end of turn."))
    print-line-uni ("shrink huge     : " & describe-effect (parse-pump-neg "Target creature gets -1/-99999999999999999999 until end of turn."))
    print-line-uni ("damage small    : " & describe-effect (parse-primary-effect "Shock deals 2 damage to any target."))
    print-line-uni ("damage huge     : " & describe-effect (parse-primary-effect "Shock deals 99999999999999999999 damage to any target."))
    print-line-uni ("whole card huge : " & describe-effect (whole-card-effect "Shock deals 99999999999999999999 damage to any target."))
    print-line-uni ("i64 max         : " & show (parse-int-prefix "9223372036854775807" 0 19 0))
    print-line-uni ("i64 max + 1     : " & show (parse-int-prefix "9223372036854775808" 0 19 0))
    print-line-uni ("find huge       : " & show (find-number "x 99999999999999999999 y" 0 24))
    print-line-uni ("token word huge : " & show (token-number "99999999999999999999"))
    print-line-uni "done"
  end
